module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.ProjDegreeOpen
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.Open

/-!
# The degree-`d` opens are compatible with the transitions of a relative Proj

For a graded ring `𝒜` the degree-`d` open of `Proj 𝒜` is the union `U_d = ⋃_{f ∈ 𝒜 d} D₊(f)` of
Equation 27.12.0.1 (`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.degreeOpen`). This file proves that those opens are
**compatible with the transition morphisms** of the relative homogeneous spectrum of a
quasi-coherent graded algebra: for affine opens `U ⊆ V` of the base, the inverse image of
`U_d ⊆ Proj Γ(V, 𝒜)` under the transition morphism of Tag 01NO is exactly `U_d ⊆ Proj Γ(U, 𝒜)`.

One of the two inclusions is formal: the transition is `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` of the
restriction map, which is a *graded* ring map, so it carries `Γ(V, 𝒜)_d` into `Γ(U, 𝒜)_d` and the
inverse image of `D₊(a)` is `D₊(a|_U)`. The other inclusion is the quasi-coherence content: a
homogeneous section of degree `d` over the smaller open has to be expressed through sections of
the *same* degree `d` over the bigger one. That is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.mem_span_res_grading` below — the degree-`d`
refinement of the span argument proving Tag 01N2 for an arbitrary inclusion of affine opens,
whose local step already produces an element of the same degree `d`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map_preimage_degreeOpen`: for a graded ring map `f : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ`, the
  inverse image of `U_d ⊆ Proj 𝒜` under `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map f` is `U_d ⊆ Proj ℬ`,
  provided every homogeneous element of `ℬ` of degree `d` lies in the ideal generated by the
  image of the degree-`d` part of `𝒜`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.mem_span_res_grading`: **the degree-`d` form of
  quasi-coherence.** For affine opens `U ⊆ V` of the base, a homogeneous section of degree `d`
  over `U` lies in the ideal of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` generated by the restrictions of the homogeneous
  sections of degree `d` over `V`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.transition_preimage_degreeOpen` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.projInclusionMap_preimage_degreeOpen`: hence the inverse
  image of the degree-`d` open along a transition morphism of Tag 01NO is the degree-`d` open,
  for the transition of a `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.GradedAlgebra` and for that of a
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.RelativeProjData.toBase_chart_apply`,
  `...RelativeProjData.chart_transition_apply` and
  `...RelativeProjData.exists_projInclusionMap_eq`: the three chart facts the locality argument on
  a relative homogeneous spectrum needs, for an arbitrary
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.RelativeProjData`.

## Implementation notes

**Universes.** `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` declares the `SetLike` carriers of the two gradings in
the universe of the rings, so `map_preimage_degreeOpen` is stated with all four types in `Type u`,
as `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.mapHomOfTop_eq_map` already is. At independent
carrier universes the statement does not elaborate — it fails with a `whnf` heartbeat timeout
while elaborating `Proj.map f hf`, not with a type error.

**Why the span statement needs no positivity.** `mem_span_res_grading` is proved for every `d`,
including `d = 0`, because the local step it rests on,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.exists_pow_mul_eq_res`, has no hypothesis on the
degree. The positivity in Tag 01N2 comes from the irrelevant ideal, not from this argument.

**The three chart facts.**
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.toBase_chart_apply` and
`...RelativeProjMapDomain.chart_transition_apply` are stated for the *constructed*
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.relativeProj`; their proofs use nothing but the two fields
`chart_isPullback` and `chart_transition`, so they are restated here for an arbitrary
`RelativeProjData`, which is the generality in which the relative degree opens are built.
`...RelativeProjMapDomain.opensRange_projInclusionMap` and the instance
`...RelativeProjMapDomain.isOpenImmersion_projInclusionMap` mention no `RelativeProjData` at all
and are used as they stand.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NQ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits HomogeneousIdeal TopologicalSpace Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Proj

variable {A B : Type u} {σ τ : Type u}
  [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
  [SetLike τ B] [AddSubgroupClass τ B]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) (ℬ : ℕ → τ) [GradedRing 𝒜] [GradedRing ℬ]

omit [AddSubgroupClass σ A] [GradedRing 𝒜] in
/-- If `b` lies in the ideal generated by the image of the degree-`d` part of `𝒜`, then `D₊(b)` is
covered by the standard opens of those images: a homogeneous prime avoiding `b` cannot contain all
of them. -/
public theorem basicOpen_le_iSup_of_mem_span (f : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ) {d : ℕ} {b : B}
    (hb : b ∈ Ideal.span ((f : A → B) '' (𝒜 d : Set A))) :
    Proj.basicOpen ℬ b ≤ ⨆ s : 𝒜 d, Proj.basicOpen ℬ (f s) := by
  intro x hx
  by_contra hnot
  rw [mem_basicOpen] at hx
  refine hx ?_
  have hsub : Ideal.span ((f : A → B) '' (𝒜 d : Set A)) ≤ x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal := by
    rw [Ideal.span_le]
    rintro y ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩
    by_contra hy
    exact hnot (TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨s, hs⟩, (mem_basicOpen ℬ _ x).mpr hy⟩)
  exact hsub hb

/-- **The degree-`d` opens are compatible with `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map`.** The inverse image of
`U_d = ⋃_{a ∈ 𝒜 d} D₊(a)` under the morphism induced by a graded ring map `f : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ` is
`U_d = ⋃_{b ∈ ℬ d} D₊(b)`, provided every homogeneous element of degree `d` of `ℬ` lies in the
ideal generated by the image of the degree-`d` part of `𝒜`.

Without the hypothesis one inclusion still holds, because `f` is graded: the inverse image of
`D₊(a)` is `D₊(f a)`, and `f a` is again of degree `d`. The hypothesis is what gives the other. -/
public theorem map_preimage_degreeOpen (f : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ) (hf : ℬ₊ ≤ 𝒜₊.map f) (d : ℕ)
    (hspan : ∀ b ∈ ℬ d, b ∈ Ideal.span ((f : A → B) '' (𝒜 d : Set A))) :
    Proj.map f hf ⁻¹ᵁ Proj.degreeOpen 𝒜 d = Proj.degreeOpen ℬ d := by
  have h1 : Proj.map f hf ⁻¹ᵁ Proj.degreeOpen 𝒜 d = ⨆ s : 𝒜 d, Proj.basicOpen ℬ (f s) := by
    rw [degreeOpen, Scheme.Hom.preimage_iSup]
    simp only [map_preimage_basicOpen]
  rw [h1]
  refine le_antisymm (iSup_le fun s => basicOpen_le_degreeOpen ℬ (f.map_mem s.2)) ?_
  rw [degreeOpen]
  exact iSup_le fun b => basicOpen_le_iSup_of_mem_span 𝒜 ℬ f (hspan b b.2)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Proj

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge

namespace RelativeProjGeneral

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (𝒜 : GradedAlgebra S)

/-- **Quasi-coherence in a single degree.** For affine opens `U ⊆ V` of the base, a homogeneous
section of degree `d` over `U` lies in the ideal of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` generated by the restrictions of the
homogeneous sections of degree `d` over `V`.

This is the degree-`d` refinement of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.irrelevant_le_map_res_of_le_opens`, Tag 01N2 for an
arbitrary inclusion: the span argument there already produces, for a homogeneous section of degree
`d`, an element of the *same* degree `d` over `V`, so the supremum over all positive degrees that
the irrelevant ideal takes is never used. The sections over `V` whose basic open lies inside `U`
generate the unit ideal of `Γ(S, U)`, and a power of each of them carries the given section into
the ideal, so a radical computation gives the section itself. -/
public theorem mem_span_res_grading {U V : S.AffineZariskiSite} (h : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens)
    {d : ℕ} {b : 𝒜.ring U} (hb : b ∈ 𝒜.grading U d) :
    b ∈ Ideal.span ((𝒜.res h) '' (𝒜.grading V d : Set (𝒜.ring V))) := by
  set I := Ideal.span ((𝒜.res h) '' (𝒜.grading V d : Set (𝒜.ring V))) with hI
  let Q : Ideal Γ(S, U.toOpens) :=
    { carrier := {x | b * 𝒜.str U x ∈ I}
      add_mem' := fun {x y} hx hy => by
        show b * 𝒜.str U (x + y) ∈ I
        rw [map_add, mul_add]
        exact I.add_mem hx hy
      zero_mem' := by
        show b * 𝒜.str U 0 ∈ I
        rw [map_zero, mul_zero]
        exact I.zero_mem
      smul_mem' := fun c x hx => by
        show b * 𝒜.str U (c • x) ∈ I
        have h2 : b * 𝒜.str U (c • x) = 𝒜.str U c * (b * 𝒜.str U x) := by
          rw [smul_eq_mul, map_mul]; ring
        rw [h2]
        exact I.mul_mem_left _ hx }
  have hQ : Q = ⊤ := by
    refine Ideal.radical_eq_top.mp (top_le_iff.mp ?_)
    rw [← span_res_sections_eq_top (S := S) h, Ideal.span_le]
    rintro g ⟨f, hfU, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨N, c, a, ha, heq⟩ := exists_pow_mul_eq_res 𝒜 h
      (W := U.basicOpen (S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op f)) (S.basicOpen_le _) f _
      (Subtype.ext (basicOpen_res_of_le h f hfU)) rfl (𝒜.res_str h f).symm hb
    refine ⟨N, ?_⟩
    show b * 𝒜.str U (S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op f ^ N) ∈ I
    rw [map_pow, heq]
    exact I.mul_mem_left c (Ideal.subset_span ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩)
  have h1 : (1 : Γ(S, U.toOpens)) ∈ Q := hQ ▸ Submodule.mem_top
  have h2 : b * 𝒜.str U (1 : Γ(S, U.toOpens)) ∈ I := h1
  rwa [map_one, mul_one] at h2

/-- **The transition morphisms are compatible with the degree-`d` opens.** For affine opens
`U ⊆ V` of the base, the inverse image under the transition morphism of Tag 01NO of the degree-`d`
open of `Proj Γ(V, 𝒜)` is the degree-`d` open of `Proj Γ(U, 𝒜)`. -/
public theorem transition_preimage_degreeOpen {U V : S.AffineZariskiSite}
    (h : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens)
    (hdom : mapDomain (𝒜.grading V) (𝒜.grading U) (𝒜.res h) = ⊤) (d : ℕ) :
    𝒜.transition h hdom ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.degreeOpen (𝒜.grading V) d =
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.degreeOpen (𝒜.grading U) d := by
  rw [𝒜.transition_eq_map h hdom (irrelevant_le_map_res_of_le_opens 𝒜 h)]
  exact AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map_preimage_degreeOpen _ _ _ _ d
    fun _ hb => mem_span_res_grading 𝒜 h hb

end RelativeProjGeneral

namespace RelativeProj

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (A : SheafGradedAlgebra S)

/-- **The transition morphisms of Tag 01NO are compatible with the degree-`d` opens of
Equation 27.12.0.1.** For affine opens `U ⊆ V` of the base, the inverse image of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.degreeOpen (A.grading V) d` under
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.projInclusionMap` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.degreeOpen (A.grading U) d`. -/
public theorem projInclusionMap_preimage_degreeOpen (U V : S.Opens) (h : U ≤ V)
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (d : ℕ) :
    projInclusionMap A U V h hU hV ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.degreeOpen (A.grading V) d =
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.degreeOpen (A.grading U) d :=
  RelativeProjGeneral.transition_preimage_degreeOpen A.toGradedAlgebra
    (U := ⟨U, hU⟩) (V := ⟨V, hV⟩) h (projInclusionDomain_eq_top A U V h hU hV) d

namespace RelativeProjData

variable {A} (P : RelativeProjData A)

/-- The base point of a point of the chart over an affine open `V` of the base, read inside `V`.

This is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.toBase_chart_apply` for an arbitrary
relative homogeneous spectrum rather than the constructed one; the proof is the commuting square
of the field `chart_isPullback`. -/
public theorem toBase_chart_apply (V : S.Opens) (hV : IsAffineOpen V)
    (z : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (A.grading V)) :
    P.toBase (P.chart V hV z) = V.ι (projInclusionToOpen A V hV z) := by
  rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, (P.chart_isPullback V hV).w, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply]

/-- The charts of a nested pair of affine opens of the base, read at a point.

This is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.chart_transition_apply` for an arbitrary
relative homogeneous spectrum rather than the constructed one; the proof is the field
`chart_transition`. As there, the equality of morphisms itself cannot be rewritten underneath the
image functor, whose `IsOpenImmersion` argument depends on it, so the pointwise form is what gets
used. -/
public theorem chart_transition_apply (W V : S.Opens) (hWV : W ≤ V)
    (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (y : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (A.grading W)) :
    P.chart V hV (projInclusionMap A W V hWV hW hV y) = P.chart W hW y := by
  rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, P.chart_transition W V hWV hW hV]

/-- A point of the chart over an affine open `V` of the base whose base point lies in a smaller
affine open `W` comes from the chart over `W`. -/
public theorem exists_projInclusionMap_eq {W V : S.Opens} (hWV : W ≤ V)
    (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (z : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (A.grading V))
    (hz : P.toBase (P.chart V hV z) ∈ W) :
    ∃ y, projInclusionMap A W V hWV hW hV y = z := by
  have hmem : z ∈ (projInclusionMap A W V hWV hW hV).opensRange := by
    rw [RelativeProjMapDomain.opensRange_projInclusionMap]
    show V.ι (projInclusionToOpen A V hV z) ∈ W
    rw [← P.toBase_chart_apply V hV z]
    exact hz
  exact hmem

end RelativeProjData

end RelativeProj

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

